  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Primary Path",
      "items": [
        "Employee input creates the version-1 claim row plus one expense_field_evidence row per supplied field, all source=employee_input",
        "PATCH /api/v1/expenses/{expense_id} appends new field evidence at version+1: employee_input for the owner, reviewer_correction for a scoped reviewer",
        "Node sublabels show route suffixes only; every path is mounted under /api/v1 and both clients may call either the expense or the receipt route"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Receipt Intake",
      "items": [
        "The multipart upload is capped by RECEIPT_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES; the real type is sniffed from magic bytes and the declared content type is never trusted",
        "Only JPEG, PNG and WebP may queue extraction - HEIC, HEIF and PDF validate against the storage allow-list but are refused for extraction",
        "Receipt bytes live in private object storage (local or supabase); content is streamed only through the authorized /receipts/{receipt_id}/content route"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Extraction Is Not Proven",
      "items": [
        "EXTRACTION_PROVIDER defaults to 'unavailable', which returns no fields, and every other unverified provider name fails closed at construction",
        "The upload persists a PENDING extraction run; the worker claims it and records UNAVAILABLE, so structured_result and validation_result stay NULL",
        "structured_result is constrained to success/partial runs, and no code path writes an expense_field_evidence row with source=receipt_extraction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Advisory, Not Persisted",
      "items": [
        "POST /api/v1/policy/check writes nothing - no finding, no decision, no status change, no audit event - and its response is labelled advisory",
        "No route or service writes a findings row yet: the evaluator returns finding drafts and names persist_findings_and_transition_status as a step, not an implementation",
        "duplicate_candidates has no writer; receipts.sha256 is the duplicate signal and only the local demo seeder links duplicate receipts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Guarantees And Limits",
      "items": [
        "audit_events refuses UPDATE and DELETE through trg_audit_events_append_only - database-enforced append-only, not cryptographic immutability",
        "An approved or rejected claim is a workflow status change; no payment or reimbursement execution exists anywhere in the backend",
        "Analytics reads persisted expenses only and never joins receipts, extraction runs, findings or audit rows, so those records cannot multiply an aggregate"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
